    "n_faq": {
      "type": "n_faq",
      "blocks": {
        "accordion_1": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What are the benefits of Micro-Infusion Pro PDRN?",
            "text": "<p>Micro-Infusion Pro PDRN combines our newly redesigned Micro-Infusion Pro device with a brand-new serum formulated with PDRN and Vitamin B12. PDRN (Polydeoxyribonucleotide) is a salmon-derived DNA ingredient popular in Korean skincare and aesthetic treatments for its skin-rejuvenating properties and ability to support healthier-looking, smoother skin. Vitamin B12 helps condition the skin and gives our serum its beautiful, naturally pink hue.</p><p>Unlike traditional topical PDRN serums, Micro-Infusion Pro uses 20 ultra-fine, 0.5 mm gold-plated needles to create tiny micro-channels while simultaneously applying the serum directly to the treated skin. Together, this innovative treatment helps:</p><ul><li>Visibly reduce the appearance of fine lines and wrinkles.</li><li>Improve uneven skin texture and smoothness.</li><li>Deeply hydrate for plumper, bouncier-looking skin.</li><li>Support a brighter, more even-looking complexion.</li><li>Leave skin looking refreshed, radiant and revitalised.</li></ul>"
          }
        },
        "accordion_2": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How quickly will I see results?",
            "text": "<p>You can expect to wake up to a beautiful, dewy glow as early as the morning after your first treatment, with skin looking more hydrated, refreshed and plump.</p><p>Consistency is key! With regular treatments every two weeks, you can expect to see more noticeable improvements over approximately three months, including smoother-looking skin texture, visibly softened fine lines and a plumper, more youthful-looking complexion. Individual results may vary.</p>"
          }
        },
        "accordion_3": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Is it painful to use?",
            "text": "<p>Not at all! Micro-Infusion Pro is designed to be virtually painless, making it an easy and comfortable at-home treatment. Its 20 ultra-fine, 0.5 mm gold-plated needles create tiny micro-channels in the skin. You may feel a slight prickling sensation during treatment, but most users find it very comfortable.</p><p>Simply use gentle, even pressure when stamping. If you have particularly sensitive skin, we recommend using lighter, gentler stamps for a more comfortable experience.</p>"
          }
        },
        "accordion_4": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How often can I use the treatment?",
            "text": "<p>We recommend using Micro-Infusion Pro PDRN once every two weeks for optimal results. Consistency is key to achieving and maintaining visible improvements in your skin’s appearance.</p>"
          }
        },
        "accordion_5": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "When is the best time to do Micro-Infusion Pro PDRN?",
            "text": "<p>We recommend using Micro-Infusion Pro PDRN every two weeks, preferably at night, to give your skin time to recover overnight. You’ll wake up to skin that looks beautifully hydrated, plump and glowing!</p><p>For detailed pre- and post-treatment skincare instructions, please refer to the product manual and our online Micro-Infusion treatment guide.</p>"
          }
        },
        "accordion_6": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Can I use it around the eyes and on the neck?",
            "text": "<p>Yes! Micro-Infusion Pro can be used on the face and neck, including carefully around the under-eye area, up to the orbital bone. Use very gentle pressure and only one pass around the eyes. Avoid the eyelids, lash line, broken skin and any areas experiencing irritation.</p>"
          }
        },
        "accordion_7": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Can I use a different serum with the Micro-Infusion Pro PDRN device?",
            "text": "<p>Micro-Infusion Pro PDRN comes pre-filled with our specially formulated PDRN serum and is ready to use straight out of the box. There’s no need to add, mix or replace the serum.</p><p>We don’t recommend using third-party serums with Micro-Infusion Pro. Every Qure serum is specifically formulated and carefully tested to work with our device, including its needle head and serum delivery system. We assess everything from serum texture and consistency to pumping performance and flow, ensuring smooth, reliable application. We can only guarantee the compatibility and tested safety of our own formulas when used as directed.</p><p>If you’re also using our Micro-Infusion Pro 2-in-1 serum, you can alternate between the two treatments every two weeks to enjoy the benefits of both formulas.</p>"
          }
        },
        "accordion_8": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How is this different from micro-rolling?",
            "text": "<p>Unlike traditional derma rollers, which use a rolling motion across the skin, Micro-Infusion Pro uses a controlled stamping action to create tiny micro-channels. This allows the specially formulated PDRN serum to be applied during treatment, combining the benefits of micro-infusion with targeted skincare ingredients. The pre-filled design also means there’s no mixing, filling or manual assembly required.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
